**Issue**: #219
**Date**: 2026-08-22
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

Feature: Harden execute against transient Herdr lifecycle races

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Expected pasted worker prompt is recovered
    Given an idle worker has no handoff and the expected deterministic worker prompt is visibly pasted
    When Herdr prompt wait settles before submission
    Then execute submits Enter and waits for the worker to enter working
    And it waits for the worker to settle idle or done before evaluating the resulting handoff

  @SCN008 @regression
  Scenario: All three leading prompt previews authorize recovery
    Given an idle worker has no handoff and detection shows "You are the", "Execute the", and "Write the h"
    When Herdr prompt wait settles before submission
    Then execute submits Enter and waits for the worker to enter working
    And it waits for the worker to settle idle or done before evaluating the resulting handoff

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Unrelated visible prompt fails closed
    Given an idle worker has no handoff and detection contains unrelated text beginning with "You are the"
    When execute evaluates prompt recovery
    Then it does not submit Enter
    And it stops with the applicable fail-closed reason

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Working worker settles before handoff validation
    Given a worker is working and has not written its handoff
    When prompt wait returns
    Then execute waits for settlement before validating the handoff

  @SCN009 @regression
  Scenario: Visible working indicator outruns agent state
    Given detection shows the worker is working while the agent state still reports idle
    When the handoff is not yet present
    Then execute waits for working and settled states without resubmitting the prompt
    And it validates the resulting handoff

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Review menus are driven as distinct transitions
    Given a review worker has `/review` pasted or Review Mode visible
    When execute starts review orchestration
    Then it submits `/review` when necessary
    And it selects PR-style review
    And it selects literal `main` from the observed base-branch menu

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: One transient worker startup failure is recovered
    Given the first agent start call fails in a controller-created pane
    When one second passes
    Then execute retries the same agent and pane once
    And continues when that retry succeeds

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Two worker startup failures stop safely
    Given both permitted agent start calls fail
    When execute evaluates startup
    Then it stops with agent_start_failed
    And leaves the worker pane open

  @SCN007 @exercise
  Scenario: Injected startup failure completes full delivery
    Given a disposable approved issue and a wrapper that fails exactly the first Herdr agent start
    When execute runs end to end
    Then all queue steps complete
    And the pull request merges and issue closes
    And no worker pane remains
